Subject: [PATCH] ctrl: a retired agent's rejoin waits for every radio it has: one Renew first, then the other missing bands, per band with a back-off, then a slow retry; a neighbor-only Topology Notification is not the agent's own activity; a rejoined model takes back its DataElements instance

0270 declared a retired agent rejoined at the first pass where its model had a radio and stopped
renewing: a 3-radio agent counted as rejoined after its first M1 (rdk-1010 and a hardware bench, 21
October: "rejoined ... 1 radios rebuilt"), and a band whose Renew or M1 was lost got no more.

The rejoin now waits for every radio the agent has: those of its retirement and those its last
Topology Response lists in its AP Operational BSS TLV; a radio of its retirement is left out only
when a response no longer lists it at all, so a radio listed with no BSS (redoing WSC) is still
waited for. A radio is back when its RUID is in the model and its em, on this model, is past M2
and not misconfigured: an AP Capability Report puts a radio in the model by RUID without an M1.

The Renews: a Renew names one band; an RDK agent sends that band's radio's M1 only (one Renew, one
M1), a Multi-AP agent may send every radio's. So one Renew first, and 5 s later the other missing
bands' at once; then per band up to three with the back-off; then, a live agent never given up on,
a Renew per missing band every 10 min, logged the first and every sixth time (a partly rejoined
agent, or one heard but sending no M1: its own side stuck). A Renew can go unanswered for a while:
a vendor extender ignored the one that came in the same second as its own Search and answered the
next. An agent heard and then unheard for 180 s starts over at its next frame. The models'
radios and listed radios are read under the topology lock, taken before the liveness lock (the
order update_network_topology takes them in), the em map's lock innermost.

A neighbor-only Topology Notification (no BSS) names the agent whose neighbors changed; the
controller's own 1905 neighbor ageing raises one for a departed agent some 60 s after its last
frame. Counted as that agent's activity it reset its silence (its retirement came about 240 s after
its last frame, not 180 s); it no longer counts, and starts no rejoin. The liveness query it
triggers still finds an agent that is there.

A rejoined agent's model made again took a new DataElements instance (Device.{i}, the model's
creation counter), leaving gaps a reader walking Device.1..N misses: it takes back the one it had,
unless another model holds it now.

The missing-radio set and the renew plan are static helpers (rejoin_missing_radios,
rejoin_plan_renew, counts_as_agent_activity) with unit tests in test_l1_em_ctrl.cpp.
